# CTF-01 literal member inputs and pre-output policy proposal

This is a source-only draft for Root's first Native input/projection freeze. It
contains literal input cases, a proposed field selection and separate variable
precision criteria. It contains no expected array, numerical evaluator, expected
method exit, engine result, scientific PASS, build command or new QA stage.
The existing card and its four gates are unchanged.

The primary source is pinned EnergyPlus26.1.0 commit
`6f2e40d10250a105b49966baa24d843711e61048`, Construction.cc59-401. The real public
method must continue through its unchanged downstream body; callbacks after309,
372 and401 only copy actual private locals. A prefix reimplementation or stopping
the method after401 cannot stand in for the Native observation.

`case-matrix.json` holds scalar bit literals, actual MaterialBase member seeds,
and ordered construction calls. Its compact references expand only input data.
Scalar bits are authoritative; decimal annotations are not expected answers.
The proposed model/call totals are derived from those arrays, not hardcoded
scientific coverage. Branch-intent labels describe source selection before any
run; they do not assert that an actual call reached or returned from a branch.

The default explicit lane uses positive finite Regular properties and genuine
NoMass-form zero property defaults with positive R. MaterialBase group is Regular
for both forms, matching the actual NoMass loader. The baseline massive R seeds
are physically consistent literals; threshold diagnostic seeds still remain
explicit member inputs, never claimed results of Material::GetMaterialData.
There are no artificial NaN/Inf or zero-thickness Regular full-call cases. No
unguarded cnd semantics are removed merely because such pathological inputs are
outside this admitted Native proposal.

The matrix covers actual active lengths1 through11, single/multiple mass layers,
boundary and interior NoMass, computed ResLayer distinct from ROnly, two/three
adjacent interior layers, disjoint runs, boundary-neighbor merge gating, and
forward/reversed literal resistance stacks. Exact binary64 threshold neighbors
exercise conductivity <=1e-6, strict thinness <1e-6, R <0.001 and thickness >3.
For thinness neighbors, binary-exact rho=1/128, cp=128 and k=1 keep the declared
property ratio at the threshold canary while respecting the IDD cp minimum100.
The comparer never evaluates this expression for an answer. Low-R error seeds
are explicitly member-level diagnostics below the IDD NoMass minimum, not
claims that a production loader accepts those IDF values.

Two groups test real shared ErrorsFound/DoCTFErrorReport references and declared
construction order. One starts with a selected loading error before valid and
unused calls. The other starts with incoming errors/report flags. These source
early-return groups avoid depending on later CTF solver flags as Rust operands.
For every model, actual incoming/outgoing whole-call flags must still be retained.
Later solver flag changes are unpaired context outside this card; do not copy
Native after-state into a Rust input to manufacture matching caller history.

Future request spelling is `ctf01-helper-cases.v1` with `model_cases` containing
`id`, `lane`, `caller`, `materials`, `constructions`, and ordered `operations`.
Caller fields are TimeStepZone/TimeStepZoneSec binary64 DTOs and initial
ErrorsFound/DoCTFErrorReport bools. Material fields are id/Name and literal
Thickness/Conductivity/Density/SpecHeat/Resistance DTOs plus ROnly. Construction
fields are id/Name, IsUsedCTF, SourceSinkPresent=false, SolutionDimensions=1,
SourceAfterLayer=0, TempAfterLayer=0, ThicknessPerpend=0 DTO, and ordered
layer_material_ids. Each operation is id/kind=calculateTransferFunction/
construction_id. The future writer derives TotLayers and real insertion indices
from actual arrays, then observes real Num/index/LayerPoint; no ID remapping hides
order. All stable real owners exist before the first call.

The original TotLayers and LayerPoint do not shrink with local merges. Only the
actual active prefix1..LayersInConstruct is observable; neither unused array
tails nor normalized material-ID labels are invented. PostLoad/PostMerge float
locals cannot be replaced by original input fields because source branches may
have changed them. The last callback also captures actual ordered-English rs,
unguarded cnd and one-dimensional dyn. Earlier phases have no dyn/rs/cnd operands.
The three checkpoints do not provide a separate per-merge event trace or sqrt
intermediate; final-array parity must not be advertised as such a trace.

`numeric-policy.json` proposes individual atol=rtol=0 profiles with exact class
and shape for every phase/variable, and bit-exact copied member inputs. This is
feasible as a strict criterion under identical binary64 operands and source
operation order, not demonstrated equality. sqrt classification, conversion
constants, cp1.007 and cp/=(CFC*1000) retain the literal source. Do not reinterpret
the contradictory cp comment or replace cnd with a safe resistance accessor.
Root must settle the profiles before first Native outputs; later differences
remain failures rather than reasons to tune tolerances.

Reached required fields missing on either or both sides fail. Unused calls,
genuine source stops and process failures retain explicit unavailable phases,
zero numeric comparisons and no PASS. An observed nonfinite local remains
present with bits/class; finiteness is not invocation/observation availability.
DoCTFErrorReport and later coefficients have no matching selected Rust owner and
remain unpaired. Whole-call return/exception/OS status is its own actual ledger,
not a substitute for reached checkpoint availability.

The production lane is separate and remains pending: fixed ordered CON15/all45
guard refs, genuine input/Material/construction loaders, actual stored Resistance
and CTF-use owners. Unit literal seeds cannot certify that pipeline. The current
Rust material/cache context lacks stored Regular Resistance and these normalized
arrays; Raw's ignored owner proposal is a future source candidate, not current
production or execution proof. CTF-02 throughCTF-10, source/sink and two-dimensional
branches, other materials, zero/>11 active counts and thermal results are excluded.

The manifest binds exact primary source bytes/ranges and the held passive
observer source protocol. These are source identities, not future compiled hashes
or approval receipts. Only stdlib input encoding/source hashing/static syntax were
used to author this package. No target imports, builds, engines, project numerical
results, binaries, canonical documents or Git were read/executed/changed.
